<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Wambu Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1700 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Ovimbundu kingdom of the central Angolan highlands whose lands became the site of the colonial city of Huambo.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Wambu (Huambo) was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovimbundu">Ovimbundu</a> kingdoms that emerged on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benguela">Benguela</a> highlands by the 18th century, alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bailundo-kingdom">Bailundo Kingdom</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viye-kingdom">Viye Kingdom</a>. Like its neighbours, it grew as a fortified raiding state with ruling lineages of mixed local and immigrant origin.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings ruled from hilltop fortresses through titled officials and village heads. Wambu's people farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and beans and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ovimbundu">Ovimbundu</a> long-distance caravans carrying slaves, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, beeswax and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> between the interior and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benguela">Benguela</a>. Detailed records of its rulers are scarce.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Wambu was drawn into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bailundo-kingdom">Bailundo</a> revolt of 1902 and occupied by Portuguese forces by 1902–03. In 1912 the Portuguese founded the city of Huambo on its lands, which became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola's</a> main cities.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1700 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:93.53%;width:4.02%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1700 CE – 1902 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Ovimbundu religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Umbundu</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Angola</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Huambo, Wambu</dd></dl></aside></div>

